      "composition": "single-ornament",
      "description": "A long horizontal etched frieze. At the centre a winged Cupid, seen from the front with his head bowed, grips the manes of two lions that crouch to either side of him; the lions' hindquarters dissolve into large acanthus volutes that curl outward, and a further volute closes each end, the left one wrapping a cluster of berries. At the far left and far right a fragment of a neighbouring shaggy lion's head, cut by the plate edge, is included. Loose dark brown ink line work; the faint paper tone of the plate area is kept at low opacity.",
