      "composition": "single-ornament",
      "description": "A long horizontal etched frieze of linked acanthus scrolls carrying four heads. From the left, a bearded old man's head facing right under a leafy wreath; a blank cartouche of knotted branches; a young woman's head facing left crowned with flowers; a central burst of large feathery acanthus leaves; a girl's head facing right with ears of grain in her hair; a round wreath of wheat and grapes enclosing a hanging pair of scales; and a youth's head facing left wreathed in vine at the right end. Loose dark brown ink; the faint paper tone of the plate is kept at low opacity.",
